How Thoughts, Words and Deeds Are Connected


What far-reaching consequences this has for us


The following, unabridged lecture "The First Step" from the Grail Message "In the Light of Truth" explains, among other things, the interaction of thoughts, words and works according to the laws of creation, i.e. the effects of our thinking, speaking and the actions that often result from them. Depending on the type of thinking we do, these can have either a beneficial or devastating effect, which then reciprocally reflects on us in a way that is either gratifying or a heavy burden. We therefore have our own spiritual and mental ascent in our own hands! Anyone who takes just this one lecture seriously and consciously and makes every effort to fulfill it will find everything else to be their own!



"The first step


  Let my word come alive in you; for this alone can bring you the benefit you need to let your spirit rise to the bright heights of the eternal gardens of God.


  It is no use knowing the Word! And even if you could say my whole message sentence by sentence from memory in order to teach yourself and your fellow human beings... it is no use if you do not act accordingly, think in the spirit of my Word and organize your whole earthly life accordingly as something that is self-evident, something that has become part of your flesh and blood and that cannot be separated from you. Only then can you draw from my message the eternal values ​​that it contains for you.


  "You will recognize them by their works !" This word of Christ applies primarily to all readers of my message! By their works means in their work, that is, in their thinking, in their everyday actions on earth! Action also includes your speaking, not just your acting; because speaking is an action whose effect you have previously underestimated. Even thoughts are part of it.


  People are accustomed to saying that thoughts are "duty-free." By this they mean to indicate that they cannot be held accountable for thoughts on earth, because they are on a level that is inaccessible to human hands.


  That is why they often play with thoughts in the most frivolous way, or better put, they play in thoughts. Unfortunately, this is often a very dangerous game, in the frivolous delusion that they can emerge from it untouched.


  In this, however, they are mistaken; for thoughts also belong to the gross material world and must under all circumstances be separated from it before a spirit is able to soar freely as soon as it has broken the connection with the earthly body.


  Therefore, always try to resonate with your thoughts in the spirit of my message, in such a way that you only want what is noble and do not descend into lowliness because you imagine that no one can see or hear it.


  Thoughts, words and outward actions all belong to the realm of the gross materiality of this creation!


  Thoughts work in the subtle gross materiality, words in the middle, and external actions take shape in the coarsest, i.e. densest gross materiality. These three types of your actions are gross material !


  But the forms of all three are closely connected, their effects are intertwined. What this means for you, how drastically it often determines the change in your being, you cannot immediately appreciate.


  It says nothing other than that a thought, working independently in its own way, can strengthen a similar kind in medium materiality and thereby bring it to more powerful forms, and then, in the same way, working further in this strengthening, can arise again to the visible, effective form in the coarsest materiality, without you yourself appearing to be directly involved in this.


  It is shocking to know this once you know the frivolity and carelessness in the thinking of these earthlings.


  You are thereby involved, without knowing it, in many deeds which one of your fellow men performs, only because he has received reinforcement of the kind I have just explained to you, which has enabled him to carry out in the crudest manner something which had hitherto been dormant within him, but which he had previously only toyed with in his thoughts.


  So many people on earth often look upon the actions of their fellow human beings with disapproval, rejecting and condemning them with anger, although they are partly responsible for them according to the eternal laws of God ! It may be a person who is a complete stranger to them and an action that they would never have carried out themselves in the most material way.


  Just imagine yourself in such processes, and then you will understand all the more why I am calling out to you in my message: "Keep the hearth of your thoughts pure, you will thereby create peace and be happy!"


  But when you have become strong enough in your own purification, there will be fewer crimes on earth than before, crimes in which many have been complicit without knowing it.


  The time and place of such acts, in which you may be complicit, are irrelevant. Even if they happen at the opposite end of the earth from where you are, in places that you have never set foot on and whose existence you have no knowledge of. Reinforcements from your mental games arrive where they discover similar species, regardless of distance, nation and country.


  Thus, over time, thoughts of hatred and envy can descend upon individuals, groups, or entire nations where they find similarities, forcing them to commit acts which, in their triggering forms, are quite different from those which first arose from your mental games.


  The effect can then be shown in the way the person committing the act feels at the time of the act. So you may have contributed to the commission of acts whose horror you yourself never really thought of, and yet you are connected with them and a part of the reaction must burden your spirit, must cling to it like a weight when it is released from the body.


  But conversely, you can also contribute even more to peace and the happiness of humanity; through pure, happy thinking, you can participate in works that are being developed by people who are far removed from you.


  Of course, the blessing flows back to you and you do not know why it comes to you.


  If you could only see once how the immutable justice of the All-Holy Will of God is always fulfilled in the automatic laws of this creation for every single thought that you entertain, you would work with all your strength to maintain the purity of your thinking!


  Only then have you become the people whom the Creator, in His work, graciously wants to lead to the knowledge that grants them eternity and allows them to become helpers in creation, who are worthy to receive the high graces intended for the human spirit in order to pass them on, transformed, in joyful and grateful transmission , to the creatures who are only able to receive them in such a transformation by man and who today remain wickedly cut off from this through the decline of the human spirit, after they could have arisen in times of better and purer vibrating humanity.


  With this you have only just brought one sentence from my message on earth to life for you!


It is the hardest   for you , which then makes everything else much easier, the fulfillment of which must already make miracle after miracle visible on earth, tangible before you.


  Once you have overcome this , there will be another danger on the way, which results from the perversion of human thinking: you will recognize in it a power which you would only too gladly press into very specific forms, so that it can serve this or that special purpose, which is made up of your own wishes!


  I want to warn you about this today ; for the danger can swallow you up, you would perish in it after you have already taken the right path.


  Beware of trying desperately to force this purity of thought , because by doing so you would force it into certain paths and your efforts would become a trick, would only be artificially forced and would never have the great effect that they should have. Your efforts would cause harm instead of benefit, because the authenticity of free feeling would be missing. It would again be an effect of your intellectual will, but never the work of your spirit! I warn against this.


  Think of my message, which tells you that all true greatness can only lie in simplicity , since true greatness is simple! You can understand the simplicity that I mean here better if you substitute the human-earthly concept of simplicity as a transition . That is perhaps closer to your ability to understand and you will hit the nail on the head.


  You cannot give your thoughts the purity I mean by will to think, but pure will must arise from your feelings in a simple and unlimited way, not pressed into a word that can only give rise to a limited concept. That must not be the case, but an all-encompassing urge for the good, which can envelop the emergence of your thoughts, penetrate them even before they take shape, is what you need.


  It is not difficult, in fact much easier than the other attempts, as long as you allow simplicity to prevail, in which the intellectual conceit of your own ability and strength cannot arise. Empty your thoughts and release the urge for noble, good things within you, then you have the basis for thinking, which comes from the will of your spirit , and what arises from this you can then leave to the intellectual work to be carried out in the densest coarse materiality. Nothing wrong can ever take shape.


  Cast away all tormenting thoughts from you, and instead trust in your spirit, which will pave its way correctly if you do not wall it up yourself. Becoming free in spirit means nothing other than letting the spirit within you go its own way! It will then have no choice but to move towards the heights, for its nature will certainly draw it upwards. Until now you have held it back so that it could no longer develop, you have thus bound its wings or wings.


  The basis for the construction of a new humanity, which you cannot and must not ignore, lies in this one sentence: Keep the hearth of your thoughts pure!


  And that is what man must begin with! That is his first task, which makes him what he must become . A model for all who strive for light and truth, who want to serve the Creator gratefully through the nature of their whole being. Whoever fulfils this no longer needs any other instructions. He is as he should be, and will thus receive the full help that awaits him in creation and leads him upwards without interruption."

 

( Grail Message , Volume 1, Lecture No. 12: "The First Step")

